<%#
  A card that IS one settings row, for the case where a card holds exactly ONE control.

  Left: the setting's name (bold) with a one-line helper caption under it. Right: the control
  itself, vertically centred on the same row. No tinted header band — sla_policies/_card.html.erb
  stays the layout for a SECTION of several fields, where a header earns its keep by naming the
  group. Using it for a single control produced a card title and description immediately above a
  near-identical field label and hint, i.e. the same idea stated twice before you reached the
  setting.

  Render it the same way as sla_policies/_card.html.erb — as a LAYOUT partial, with the control
  supplied as the block. Locals: title; description optional. The block is the control, plus
  anything that belongs directly under it (e.g. a dependent field the control reveals).

  NOTE FOR FUTURE EDITS OF THIS COMMENT: never write a percent-greater-than sequence in here. ERB
  ends a comment at the FIRST one it meets, so an illustrative snippet containing a closing tag
  terminates the comment early and dumps the rest of it onto the page as visible text. That is
  exactly what happened to the first version of this file.
%>
<%# tw-border-solid, not just tw-border: Preflight is disabled in this plugin (CLAUDE.md), so %>
<%# nothing sets a default border-style and a width-only utility would draw no border at all. %>
<div class="tw-bg-white tw-border tw-border-solid tw-border-gray-200 tw-rounded-lg tw-shadow-sm tw-mb-5">
  <%# tw-items-center is the whole point of the row: the control sits on the label's optical %>
  <%# centre, not at the top of a two-line block. It wraps to stacked at narrow widths, where %>
  <%# label-beside-control has no room to be a row at all. %>
  <div class="tw-flex tw-flex-wrap tw-items-center tw-justify-between tw-gap-x-6 tw-gap-y-3 tw-px-5 tw-py-4">
    <div class="tw-min-w-0 tw-flex-1">
      <%# tw-m-0 / tw-mb-0: Preflight is disabled, so Purplemine2's own p margins are still in %>
      <%# force and would otherwise space this row out of proportion. %>
      <p class="tw-m-0 tw-text-base tw-font-semibold tw-text-gray-900"><%= title %></p>
      <% if local_assigns[:description].present? %>
        <p class="tw-mt-1 tw-mb-0 tw-text-sm tw-text-gray-500"><%= description %></p>
      <% end %>
    </div>
    <div class="tw-flex-shrink-0"><%= yield %></div>
  </div>
</div>
